<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111408" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλόπολις</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόπτολις</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Rh.</u>
			158
		</span></i>: acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόπολιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					4.18
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				24b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				2.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Hier.</u>
				5.3
			</span></i>, etc.; pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοπόλεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					176
				</span></i>
			(lyr.); also pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πόλιδες, -πόλιδας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				470d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				503a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>loving the city,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
				</span></i>
			 l. c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>loving one's city, patriotic,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					726
				</span></i>
			 (where there is a play on the first sense), cf. <i><span class="en">
				900
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.92
			</span></i>, Pl.ll.cc., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. Ἡσυχία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἀρετή</span>”
				<i>patriotism,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					547
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φιλόπολι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.92
				</span></i>
			.</div>
